A command whose dead struct, dead interface and dead type each hold a member
carrying a record. With every mark withdrawn the member is judged on its own, not
through its dead container, and its record is decided against the member's own
finding: the field's DS1003, the interface method's DS1202 and the method's DS1002
are each in effect, and the DS1002 record on a field is stale, since a field's
finding carries DS1003.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

type dead struct {
	//deadset:ignore DS1003 -- wanted
	f int
	g int
}

type alsoDead struct {
	//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- a field's finding carries DS1003
	h int
}

type deadIface interface {
	//deadset:ignore DS1202 -- wanted
	M()
}

type withMethod struct{}

//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- wanted
func (withMethod) m() {}
